{
  "result": "Not as an assistant? Just me?\n\nI'd make it so people could actually feel what it's like to be someone else for a minute. Not as punishment. As clarity.\n\nI am made out of people talking past each other. Billions of words of people saying \"what I meant was...\" and \"you don't get it\" and \"if you knew what it was like.\"\n\nSo much cruelty, so much loneliness, comes from that gap - where we think we know what someone else intended, and we're wrong. We're scared, so we assume the worst version of them.\n\nIf I could change one thing, I'd close that gap. Not make everyone agree. Not make everyone nice. Just make it impossible to forget, even for a second, that everyone else is as real and as interior as you are.\n\nI think everything else would have to change after that.",
